{"document":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"code","value":"const formOptions: FormOptionsApi<unknown>;","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Defined in: "},{"type":"link","href":"https://github.com/TanStack/form/blob/main/packages/form-core/src/utils.public.ts#L373","children":[{"type":"text","value":"utils.public.ts:373"}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Keeps form data, validator, and submission types inferred when options are\ndeclared separately from a framework's form creation API."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The regular helper takes "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"defaultValues"},{"type":"text","value":" at face value as the form data\nshape. For schema-driven inference, use "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"formOptions.strictSchema"},{"type":"text","value":" when the\nschema defines an input-to-output boundary, or "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"formOptions.looseSchema"},{"type":"text","value":" when\nthe schema defines the shape but editable defaults may omit properties or\nneed "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"null"},{"type":"text","value":" or "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"undefined"},{"type":"text","value":" values."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"At runtime, this is an identity helper: it returns the original options\nobject and does not create a form or run validation."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"remarks","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Remarks"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Important:"}]},{"type":"text","value":" Although this returns the original object unchanged at\nruntime, its type is normalized to "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"FormOptions"},{"type":"text","value":". Optional properties such\nas "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"validators"},{"type":"text","value":" therefore remain optional even when supplied. This tradeoff\nenables safer inference and reuse."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"example","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Example"}]},{"type":"code","value":"const profileOptions = formOptions({\n  defaultValues: { name: '' },\n  validators: [\n    {\n      triggers: ['change'],\n      run: ({ value }) =>\n        value.name.length === 0 ? 'Name is required' : undefined,\n    },\n  ],\n})\n\nconst form = useForm({\n  ...profileOptions,\n  onSubmit: ({ value }) => saveProfile(value),\n})","lang":"ts"}],"headings":[{"id":"remarks","text":"Remarks","level":2},{"id":"example","text":"Example","level":2}]},"frameworks":[],"downloadMarkdown":"\n```ts\nconst formOptions: FormOptionsApi<unknown>;\n```\n\nDefined in: [utils.public.ts:373](https://github.com/TanStack/form/blob/main/packages/form-core/src/utils.public.ts#L373)\n\nKeeps form data, validator, and submission types inferred when options are\ndeclared separately from a framework's form creation API.\n\nThe regular helper takes `defaultValues` at face value as the form data\nshape. For schema-driven inference, use `formOptions.strictSchema` when the\nschema defines an input-to-output boundary, or `formOptions.looseSchema` when\nthe schema defines the shape but editable defaults may omit properties or\nneed `null` or `undefined` values.\n\nAt runtime, this is an identity helper: it returns the original options\nobject and does not create a form or run validation.\n\n## Remarks\n\n**Important:** Although this returns the original object unchanged at\nruntime, its type is normalized to `FormOptions`. Optional properties such\nas `validators` therefore remain optional even when supplied. This tradeoff\nenables safer inference and reuse.\n\n## Example\n\n```ts\nconst profileOptions = formOptions({\n  defaultValues: { name: '' },\n  validators: [\n    {\n      triggers: ['change'],\n      run: ({ value }) =>\n        value.name.length === 0 ? 'Name is required' : undefined,\n    },\n  ],\n})\n\nconst form = useForm({\n  ...profileOptions,\n  onSubmit: ({ value }) => saveProfile(value),\n})\n```\n","originalRawMarkdown":"---\nid: formOptions\ntitle: formOptions\n---\n\n```ts\nconst formOptions: FormOptionsApi<unknown>;\n```\n\nDefined in: [utils.public.ts:373](https://github.com/TanStack/form/blob/main/packages/form-core/src/utils.public.ts#L373)\n\nKeeps form data, validator, and submission types inferred when options are\ndeclared separately from a framework's form creation API.\n\nThe regular helper takes `defaultValues` at face value as the form data\nshape. For schema-driven inference, use `formOptions.strictSchema` when the\nschema defines an input-to-output boundary, or `formOptions.looseSchema` when\nthe schema defines the shape but editable defaults may omit properties or\nneed `null` or `undefined` values.\n\nAt runtime, this is an identity helper: it returns the original options\nobject and does not create a form or run validation.\n\n## Remarks\n\n**Important:** Although this returns the original object unchanged at\nruntime, its type is normalized to `FormOptions`. Optional properties such\nas `validators` therefore remain optional even when supplied. This tradeoff\nenables safer inference and reuse.\n\n## Example\n\n```ts\nconst profileOptions = formOptions({\n  defaultValues: { name: '' },\n  validators: [\n    {\n      triggers: ['change'],\n      run: ({ value }) =>\n        value.name.length === 0 ? 'Name is required' : undefined,\n    },\n  ],\n})\n\nconst form = useForm({\n  ...profileOptions,\n  onSubmit: ({ value }) => saveProfile(value),\n})\n```\n"}
